; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Curve Stitching
; CATEGORY: Spirals & Curves
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     string art, parabola, straight lines, for loop
; SUMMARY:  Joins evenly spaced marks on two straight lines to sew a smooth curve out of nothing but straight threads.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Take two lines that meet at a corner. Mark 20 equal steps on
;   each. Join mark 1 on the first line to mark 20 on the second,
;   mark 2 to mark 19, and so on. Every thread is straight, yet a
;   smooth curve (a parabola) appears where they cross. Four such
;   corners round a cross make a four-pointed star.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change MARKS for more or fewer threads.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * FOR counts through the marks
;   * finding the k-th mark on a line by moving k equal steps
;   * how many straight lines can outline a curve (an "envelope")
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Use 40 marks. Is the curve smoother?
;   * Open the corner wider: draw the lines at 120 degrees.
;   * Draw it with yarn and a needle on card, like children did 100 years ago.
; ============================================================

make "marks 20

; Stitch between two arms that start at the same corner point.
; Arm A goes from the corner to point a, arm B from the corner to point b.
; Mark k on arm A is k / marks of the way along it.
to stitch :corner :a :b :color
  setpencolor :color
  for [k 0 :marks] [
    localmake "t :k / :marks
    penup setpos between :corner :a :t
    pendown setpos between :corner :b 1 - :t
  ]
end

; The point a fraction :t of the way from p to q.
to between :p :q :t
  output list (first :p) + :t * ((first :q) - (first :p)) (last :p) + :t * ((last :q) - (last :p))
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [250 246 236]
setpensize 1.5
; four corners, each made of half of the horizontal and half of the
; vertical line of a big cross
stitch [0 0] [0 270] [270 0] [200 50 80]
stitch [0 0] [270 0] [0 -270] [230 140 30]
stitch [0 0] [0 -270] [-270 0] [40 140 120]
stitch [0 0] [-270 0] [0 270] [60 90 200]
